text:
Message Contract

Host -&gt; MFE
{
  type: "BRDR_ALIGNMENT_INIT",
  payload: {
    crs: "EPSG:31370" | "EPSG:3812" | "EPSG:28992",
    geometry: GeoJSONGeometry
  }
}
Optional update while the MFE stays open:
{
  type: "BRDR_ALIGNMENT_UPDATE_GEOMETRY",
  payload: {
    crs: "EPSG:31370" | "EPSG:3812" | "EPSG:28992",
    geometry: GeoJSONGeometry
  }
}
Important:

send a GeoJSON Geometry, not a full FeatureCollection
the coordinates must match the CRS you pass in payload.crs
supported geometry types are Point, MultiPoint, LineString, MultiLineString, Polygon, MultiPolygon



MFE -&gt; Host
Ready event:
{ type: "BRDR_ALIGNMENT_READY" }
Apply event:
{
  type: "BRDR_ALIGNMENT_APPLY",
  payload: {
    geometry: GeoJSONGeometry
  }
}

Minimal Example
&lt;iframe
  id="brdr-mfe"
  src="https://example.com/alignment-mfe.html?hostOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fhost.example.com"
  style="width:100%;height:800px;border:0"
  sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin"
&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
  const iframe = document.getElementById("brdr-mfe");
  const mfeOrigin = "https://example.com";

  const selectedGeometry = {
    type: "Polygon",
    coordinates: [[[674109.9, 679157.1], [674108.4, 679157.3], [674067.2, 679162.5], [674109.9, 679157.1]]]
  };

  window.addEventListener("message", (event) =&gt; {
    if (event.origin !== mfeOrigin) return;
    const msg = event.data;
    if (!msg || typeof msg !== "object") return;

    if (msg.type === "BRDR_ALIGNMENT_READY") {
      iframe.contentWindow.postMessage(
        {
          type: "BRDR_ALIGNMENT_INIT",
          payload: {
            crs: "EPSG:3812",
            geometry: selectedGeometry
          }
        },
        mfeOrigin
      );
    }

    if (msg.type === "BRDR_ALIGNMENT_APPLY") {
      const alignedGeometry = msg.payload.geometry;
      console.log("Aligned geometry", alignedGeometry);
    }
  });
&lt;/script&gt;

POST /aligner
Returns the viewer-oriented BRDR output structure.
Query parameter:

feature_id (optional): required when request contains multiple features
result_mode=all (default) or result_mode=predictions
include_metadata=true (optional): also returns raw BRDR metadata in the response

Request body (shape):
{
  "featurecollection": {
    "type": "FeatureCollection",
    "features": [
      {
        "type": "Feature",
        "id": "2",
        "properties": {
          "metadata": {
            "actuation": "created",
            "observations": ["first"]
          }
        },
        "geometry": {
          "type": "Polygon",
          "coordinates": [[[0,0],[1,0],[1,1],[0,1],[0,0]]]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "params": {
    "crs": "EPSG:31370",
    "reference_loader": "grb",
    "grb_type": "GRB - ADP - administratief perceel",
    "reference_url": null,
    "reference_id_property": null,
    "reference_typename": null,
    "reference_collection": null,
    "reference_partition": 1000,
    "reference_limit": 10000,
    "full_reference_strategy": "prefer_full_reference",
    "od_strategy": "SNAP_ALL_SIDE",
    "snap_strategy": "PREFER_VERTICES",
    "max_relevant_distance": 6.0,
    "processor": "AlignerGeometryProcessor"
  }
}
Notes:

geometry.type can be Point, LineString, Polygon and multi-variants.
max_relevant_distance is limited to 25.
reference_loader:

grb: uses grb_type
wfs: requires reference_url, reference_id_property, reference_typename
ogc_feature_api: requires reference_url, reference_id_property, reference_collection

properties is optional. When present, it can be used to pass lifecycle metadata to BRDR.
The GeoLifecycleManager viewer sends this metadata by default for subsequent versions, but the request remains valid when properties is empty.
Supported metadata forms:

nested properties.metadata
flattened properties.actuation
flattened properties.observations
flattened properties.reference_version

Existing geometry-only requests remain valid. If properties is omitted or empty, the endpoint behaves as before.

{
  "series": {
    "0.0": {
      "result": { "type": "Polygon", "coordinates": [] },
      "result_diff_min": { "type": "Polygon", "coordinates": [] },
      "result_diff_plus": { "type": "Polygon", "coordinates": [] }
    }
  },
  "diffs": {
    "0.0": 0.0
  },
  "diff_metric": "area",
  "predictions": {
    "0.0": false
  },
  "prediction_scores": {
    "0.0": 0.0
  },
  "metadata": {
    "0.0": {
      "alignment_date": "2025-02-13",
      "brdr_version": "0.8.1"
    }
  }
}
